 "what_this_proves": "For each (group j, lane k, nibble half) the PL computes nibble*q8*scale exactly for ALL 2^8 x 2^8 x 2^6 operand values, with the partner scale set to a different value (so a swapped scale mapping would fail) and all other q8 elements zero. Accumulation across lanes/groups/sub-blocks is checked at both extremes and on random full blocks (E2). Compositionality of the adder tree (that per-lane exactness plus exact int32 addition without overflow yields exact sums) is an argument about the C source, trusted through the HLS/Vivado toolchain; it is NOT enumerated here."
